# What the mutation runner needs beyond Python itself, pinned, in a file a bot
# can edit.
#
# The runner is internal/guard/mutation/mutate.py, and CI runs it from
# .github/workflows/mutation.yml. It uses psutil for one thing: watching the
# memory of the whole process tree an entry starts, so that a mutation which
# removes a limit cannot take the machine down with it. It is never linked into
# either binary and go.mod never sees it.
#
# Licence read from the pinned version rather than recalled, on 2026-10-15:
# BSD-3-Clause, stated by the wheel metadata and carried in full in the LICENSE
# file beside it.
#
# requirements-mutation.txt next to this file is compiled from it by
# pip-compile, the same way requirements-semgrep.txt is, so Dependabot proposes
# a set pip can install. To compile it by hand, from the root of the
# repository:
#
#   docker run --rm -v "$PWD/.github:/w" -w /w python:3.14-slim sh -c "pip install -q pip==26.1.1 pip-tools==7.5.3 && pip-compile --strip-extras --no-emit-index-url --output-file=requirements-mutation.txt requirements-mutation.in"
psutil==7.2.2
